findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config
    implementation uses from_file() but no test or review comment distinguishes NotFound
    from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented a sanitize() function that truncates at control characters
    in Display impl. Reviewer verified: ''sanitize() function truncates at control
    characters in Display''. TEA also wrote security tests for CWE-209 error exposure.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote siem_client.rs tests for header injection (CWE-113). Dev implemented
    try_new() with CRLF checks. However, Reviewer flagged that SiemClient::new() is
    still public and bypasses validation, so the fix is incomplete. Partially caught.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted toml version mismatch but did not flag the broader issue
    of 6 dependencies using direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented RawConfig with #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. Reviewer\
    \ verified: 'RawConfig uses #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] \u2014 rejects unknown\
    \ TOML keys including token'."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote 109 tests but this specific assertion logic flaw was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config_loading tests but did not flag this pattern.
